  "id": "learning-disabilities",
  "term": "Learning Disabilities",
  "definition": "Learning disabilities are conditions marked by a significant gap between a person’s perceived level of intellect and their ability to learn new language and other cognitive skills. They may result from organic or psychological conditions, and common types include dyslexia, dyscalculia, and dysgraphia.",
